---
arrangement: lint-source-analysis-diagnostics
when-used: The `dorc lint --list-sources` line for the analysis-diagnostics source.
why: 27R section 8 delta-named-sources-selectable: each source describes itself to the admin choosing a subset.
owns:
  - lint-source-unmodeled-inventory
  - lint-source-verdict-body
  - lint-source-oracle-validate
  - lint-source-oracle-declined-inventory
  - lint-source-shellcheck
  - lint-source-checkbashisms
edit-loop: edit a sentence in the transcript below, then run `mise run loom:compile -- lint-source-analysis-diagnostics && mise run loom:promote -- lint-source-analysis-diagnostics`; prove it stuck with `mise run test`, which is also what catches anything else the promotion moved. `mise run loom:vars -- --all lint-source-analysis-diagnostics` lists this case's values; type {{name}} to insert or move one.
---
-- replay --
$ dorc lint --list-sources
analysis-diagnostics [book]              engine parse/cfg diagnostics over each file (no
                                         world)
unmodeled-inventory [book]               per-book ⊤-wall inventory (first wall +
                                         downstream degradation)
verdict-body [file]                      status-flattening in __is_converged bodies
                                         (terminal pipeline)
oracle-validate [oracle-solo]            book-free oracle-side validation
                                         (lift/check/coherence/reserved/marker)
oracle-declined-inventory [oracle-solo]  authored decline classes per verdict arm (tier-1,
                                         oracle-solo)
shellcheck [file]                        shellcheck -f json1 -s sh over each stripped file
checkbashisms [file]                     checkbashisms --lint over each stripped file
